---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../../../styles/growth-editorial.css';
const title="Keqiao Fabric Market and Textile Supplier Visits";
const description="Prepare a Keqiao fabric sourcing trip: compare market samples, record fabric specifications and arrange confirmed textile supplier visits in Shaoxing.";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} crumbs={[{href:"/destinations/",label:"Destinations"}]} current={title} cta={false}>
<article class="growth-article keqiao-page">
<header><p class="eyebrow">Shaoxing · Zhejiang</p><h1>Keqiao fabric market and textile supplier visits</h1><p class="lead">Start at the market to compare fabrics. Arrange a separate production visit when you need to understand who makes the cloth and how your specification will be produced.</p><p>China Textile City is in Keqiao district, Shaoxing, Zhejiang. The regional textile industry includes weaving, dyeing and other production stages. A market address alone does not establish that a seller owns a mill.</p></header>
<nav class="jump-links" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#brief">Prepare your fabric brief</a><a href="#route">Market to mill</a><a href="#confirm">Confirm before travel</a></nav>
<section id="brief"><h2>Bring a specification you can compare</h2><p>Use a physical reference sample where possible. Record each quote against the same requirements, and label swatches before moving to the next supplier.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Fabric sourcing brief</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Record</th><th scope="col">Clarify with the supplier</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">End use and construction</th><td>Garment, upholstery or another use; woven or knitted construction; required composition.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Weight and width</th><td>Your target and acceptable variation; usable width and the unit used in the quote.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Colour and finish</th><td>Reference sample, colour approval, printing or finishing needs and sample approval steps.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Quantity</th><td>Quantity per colour or design; stock availability versus a new production run; MOQ.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Performance requirements</th><td>Your intended market and required test methods or results. Agree specialist testing where needed.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Delivery and traceability</th><td>Lead-time assumptions, sample reference, seller identity and the production stages to verify.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div></section>
<section id="route"><h2>Move from a market shortlist to a confirmed visit</h2><ol class="keqiao-steps">
<li><h3>Compare samples and collect records</h3><p>Record the stall or showroom, contact, swatch reference and quote assumptions together. Ask whether the offer is for stock fabric or production to order.</p></li>
<li><h3>Clarify the seller's role</h3><p>Ask who weaves or knits the fabric and who dyes, prints or finishes it. The work may involve several businesses. Confirm which site is relevant to your question before asking for a visit.</p></li>
<li><h3>Arrange the production appointment</h3><p>Confirm the address, host, permitted areas and whether the process you want to see will be running. Do not plan on same-day access simply because the market and supplier are in the same region.</p></li>
<li><h3>Compare against the same brief</h3><p>Use the <a href="/tools/factory-visit-scorecard/">supplier comparison template</a> for the evidence and open questions. Keep the approved sample and specification linked to later quotations.</p></li>
</ol></section>
<section id="confirm"><h2>Confirm these details before travelling</h2><div class="two-up"><article><h3>Market appointment</h3><p>Ask for the specific market building, floor, stall or showroom and opening hours for your date. “China Textile City” is not a sufficiently precise meeting point.</p><p>Allow time for comparing materials rather than booking every hour with a different seller.</p></article><article><h3>Production appointment</h3><p>Confirm travel from your hotel or market, visitor requirements and the production schedule. Ask about seasonal or holiday changes directly.</p><p>Get permission before filming or photographing. Access to a sales area does not include access to production.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="note"><h2>Plan the visit around the fabric</h2><p>Send your fabric specification, quantities, dates and any existing supplier contacts. We can review what needs checking and which appointments would support your decision.</p><p><a href="/contact/">Discuss a Keqiao sourcing visit</a></p></section>
<section class="regional-sources"><h2>Regional sources</h2><p class="meta">Regional background checked 15 October 2026. These sources describe the market and textile industry; they do not verify individual suppliers or appointment availability.</p><ul><li><a href="https://www.ezhejiang.gov.cn/shaoxing/2025-04/03/c_1084790.htm">Zhejiang government portal: China Textile City in Keqiao</a> (3 April 2025).</li><li><a href="https://www.ezhejiang.gov.cn/shaoxing/2025-02/05/c_1069447.htm">Zhejiang government portal: Keqiao textile production and trade</a> (5 February 2025).</li></ul></section>
<div class="related"><a href="/china-trade-fairs/#filters=city%3DShaoxing%2B%2528Keqiao%2529">Keqiao textile fair — dates and details</a><a href="/destinations/zhejiang/">Other Zhejiang destinations</a><a href="/tools/china-manufacturing-hub-finder/">Find regions by product</a><a href="/guides/questions-to-ask-china-factory-visit/">Questions for your supplier</a></div></article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
